let me start with the most weighted  point on our agenda the package of Risk  Reduction measures in the banking  industry I'm very happy to report it  after dozens of sleepless nights by the  members of the presidency team many  meetings and discussions we finally  reached an agreement among member states  we believe this is success because the  package of four files is one of the  stepping stones - about completing the  banking union the proposals agreed today  seek to implement the reforms agreed at  international level following the  financial crisis these measures will  ensure that any outstanding challenges  of financial stability are correctly  addressed let me congratulate the  Bulgarian presidency on the general  approach reached on the 2016 banking  package this package is a key  deliverable in risk reduction in the  banking sector it aims to complete the  post crisis regulatory agenda and  address outstanding issues for financial  stability and introduce internationally  agreed standards in EU legislation as  regards our anti tax avoidance gender so  we welcome that today ministers gave the  final green light on --use new tax  transparency rules for tax  intermediaries these rules will come  into force in 2020 and will provide more  transparency on the role of  intermediaries who sell products and tax  structures that can potentially help  clients to avoid tax
 

